From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:40:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally keep two commands of a
 class in flight

G16 publishes one render and one compute command at a time. Each class
has two storage owners, but every compute command names firmware UMA
slot 1 and every render command UMA slot 33, so the two owners take
turns binding ONE firmware slot: the firmware keeps it bound to the
last publisher's descriptor, free list and pool table until the next
publication rebinds it. The slot ledger therefore lets one owner be in
flight and reuses an owner only after a later owner of the slot has
fully retired. On the same GPU under macOS light commands overlap: 22 us
per compute command at depth against our 197 us.

Add two switches, both default 0 (no change):

g16_uma_split, read once at the first slot use of the boot (a module
option): owner k binds its own firmware UMA slot, compute 1 + k and
render 33 + k, inside the per-class ranges of the 25G83 layout. The
render descriptor check follows the owner's slot.

g16_overlap (runtime): with the split latched, a fully retired owner is
reusable at once and the other owner may publish meanwhile, so two
commands of a class are in flight, each on its own slot. Without the
split it has no effect, so no firmware slot is ever bound by two owners
in flight. Retirement stays oldest first in both modes.

What remains unproven, and is why both are off by default: that the
firmware does not touch an idle, completed owner's own slot before that
owner publishes again.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
